        <mxCell id="c53" value="&lt;i&gt;the continuing tests&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="781" y="713" width="79" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c54" value="&lt;i&gt;Each card is a requirement of the case, in the order of its three phases; the tags name the tools it uses (Requirement 9 is a written report built on the workbook). The teal boxes are the three milestones an instructor may collect and check. Arrows show how results move: Copy with Headers from the script into the workbook, the refund flags exported to CSV from the script into the Power BI report, Chapter 16&#x27;s register into the updated monitoring file, and the workbook, the report and the register into the committee&#x27;s report.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="835" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
